  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ixoside may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. Ixoside is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, Calysolin IV, and 1,7-Dimethylbicyclo[2.2.1]heptan-2-ol, all of which are implicated in targeting CD276 antigen. These findings indicate that Ixoside could potentially exert its biological effects by interacting with CD276 antigen through these intermediates. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with slight variations in the strength of the evidence across the three paths. The consistency in the target relationships, despite minor differences in scores, supports the hypothesis that Ixoside may play a role in modulating CD276 antigen activity. The mechanism is likely mediated through the interaction of Ixoside with these molecular targets, which in turn influence CD276 antigen function. The evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
